   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the elder law, in relation to social model adult day services\nprograms",
    "basePrintNo": "S9356",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9356-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §215, Eld L",
    "lawSection": "Elder Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9356\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the elder law, in relation to social model adult day\nservices programs\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to enhance the State Office for the Aging's\n(SOFA) oversight capacity of social adult day care programs.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one specifies that the rules and regulations promulgated by the\nDirector of SOFA apply to all social adult day care programs, regardless\nof their source of funding. This section requires the Director to\ninspect each social adult day care program to ensure the program has met\nthe standards and requirements established by the Director prior to\noperating and no less than once every five years.  No social adult day\ncare program would be eligible for funding under section 215 of the\nelder law or any other public funding. This section would also require\neach social adult day care program to conduct an annual self-certifica-\ntion beginning January first, 2030.\n\nSection two sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2023, the Assembly Aging Committee held a hearing to review and exam-\nine the oversight of social adult day care programs. The Committee\nsought to gather testimony on the current oversight of social adult day\ncare programs and ways to improve such programs for participants, their\ncaregivers, and providers. Based on the feedback from stakeholders, this\nbill seeks to enhance and strengthen the State Office for the Aging's\nauthority to regulate and oversee social adult day care programs.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
